{
 "file": "groot.mdx",
 "units": [
  {
   "id": 0,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 1924,
   "end": 1938,
   "text": "# GR00T Policy",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 1940,
   "end": 2201,
   "text": "GR00T is an NVIDIA foundation model family for generalized humanoid robot reasoning and skills. It is a cross-embodiment policy that accepts multimodal input, including language, images, and proprioception, to perform manipulation tasks in diverse environments.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2203,
   "end": 2265,
   "text": "LeRobot integrates GR00T N1.7 through the ⟦0⟧ policy type.",
   "tokens": [
    "`groot`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "kind": "quote",
   "start": 2267,
   "end": 2697,
   "text": "> [!WARNING]\n> **Breaking change:** GR00T N1.5 support was removed from LeRobot, and current releases support GR00T N1.7 only. N1.5 checkpoints and configs are rejected with a migration note. To keep using an N1.5 checkpoint, pin the last release that supports it: ⟦0⟧. To use the current release, migrate to GR00T N1.7 (base model [⟦1⟧](⟦2⟧)).",
   "tokens": [
    "`pip install 'lerobot==0.5.1'`",
    "`nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B`",
    "https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2699,
   "end": 2716,
   "text": "## Model Overview",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2718,
   "end": 2828,
   "text": "GR00T N1.7 uses a Cosmos-Reason2/Qwen3-VL backbone and provides checkpoints for SimplerEnv, DROID, and LIBERO.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2830,
   "end": 2966,
   "text": "Developers and researchers can post-train GR00T with their own real or synthetic data to adapt it for specific humanoid robots or tasks.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2968,
   "end": 3140,
   "text": "GR00T uses pre-trained vision and language encoders with a flow matching action transformer to model a chunk of actions conditioned on vision, language, and proprioception.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3319,
   "end": 3428,
   "text": "Its strong performance comes from being trained on an expansive and diverse humanoid dataset, which includes:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3430,
   "end": 3463,
   "text": "- Real captured data from robots.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3464,
   "end": 3526,
   "text": "- Synthetic data generated using NVIDIA Isaac GR00T Blueprint.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3527,
   "end": 3555,
   "text": "- Internet-scale video data.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3557,
   "end": 3683,
   "text": "This approach allows the model to be highly adaptable through post-training for specific embodiments, tasks, and environments.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3685,
   "end": 3713,
   "text": "## Installation Requirements",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3715,
   "end": 3806,
   "text": "GR00T is intended for NVIDIA GPU-accelerated systems. Install LeRobot with the GR00T extra:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3850,
   "end": 3872,
   "text": "For a source checkout:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3913,
   "end": 3921,
   "text": "## Usage",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3923,
   "end": 3941,
   "text": "To use GR00T N1.7:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3976,
   "end": 3987,
   "text": "## Training",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3989,
   "end": 4017,
   "text": "### Training Command Example",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4019,
   "end": 4110,
   "text": "Here's a complete training command for finetuning the base GR00T model on your own dataset:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4112,
   "end": 4348,
   "text": "This command is using the ⟦0⟧ flag, which is used for the SO-101 robot, [read more about how GR00T handles different embodiments.](⟦1⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "`new_embodiment`",
    "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/getting_started/policy.md#--embodiment-tag"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5469,
   "end": 5491,
   "text": "## Performance Results",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5493,
   "end": 5521,
   "text": "### LIBERO Benchmark Results",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "kind": "quote",
   "start": 5523,
   "end": 5614,
   "text": "> [!NOTE]\n> Follow the [LIBERO](⟦0⟧) setup instructions before running ⟦1⟧.",
   "tokens": [
    "./libero",
    "`lerobot-eval`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5616,
   "end": 5782,
   "text": "GR00T N1.7 has demonstrated strong performance on the LIBERO benchmark suite. To reproduce LeRobot results, follow the instructions in the [LIBERO](⟦0⟧) section.",
   "tokens": [
    "./libero"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5784,
   "end": 5803,
   "text": "### Train on LIBERO",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5805,
   "end": 5873,
   "text": "Example training command for a LIBERO suite (here ⟦0⟧):",
   "tokens": [
    "`libero_spatial`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7204,
   "end": 7320,
   "text": "This will follow the recipe found [here](⟦0⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/examples/LIBERO/README.md"
   ]
  },
  {
